%description:
Tests the data of a Fast Open SYN that the SYN-ACK does not acknowledge, when
it needs more than one segment. The first connection gets the cookie and
caches the MSS of the server, 1460 bytes. The second connection sends 1400
bytes on its SYN; the client's own MSS is 536 bytes. The tester removes the
data from the SYN, as a server that drops it, so the SYN-ACK acknowledges only
the SYN. The client sends the 1400 bytes again in three segments, within its
initial window of one segment and the growth at each ACK. The last, partial
segment goes at the second ACK (A006 at t=0.709): it is a retransmission,
which Nagle does not hold. Before, it waited for the retransmission timeout
(t=1.913).

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.fastOpen=true
*.cli_app.tOpen2=0.5s
*.cli_app.active2=true
*.cli_app.localPort2=1001
*.cli_app.tSend2=0.5s
*.cli_app.sendBytes2=1400B
*.cli_app.fastOpen2=true
*.srv_app.tOpen2=0.5s
*.srv_app.localPort2=2000

*.tcptester.script="a3 strip 34; a3 nodata"
*.srv_tcp.mss = 1460
*.cli_tcp.mss = 536
*.cli_tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.srv_tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[0.501 A003] A.1001 > B.2000: S 125000:125000(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize NOP NOP FastOpen(cookieLen=8)# removing the payload
srv_tcp: LISTEN --> SYN_RCVD  (on RCV_SYN)
[0.503 B002] A.1001 < B.2000: A S 125500:125500(0) ack 125001 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize
cli_tcp: SYN_SENT --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_SYN_ACK)
[0.505 A004] A.1001 > B.2000: A 125001:125537(536) ack 125501 win 16384 
srv_tcp: SYN_RCVD --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_ACK)
[0.707 B003] A.1001 < B.2000: A ack 125537 win 16384 
[0.709 A005] A.1001 > B.2000: A 125537:126073(536) ack 125501 win 16384 
[0.709 A006] A.1001 > B.2000: A 126073:126401(328) ack 125501 win 16384 
[0.911 B004] A.1001 < B.2000: A ack 126401 win 16384 
[0.912] tcpdump finished, A:6 B:4 segments
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
